The deprecated 2023 Production Deploy Runbook said: “A deploy can be rolled back with a single click in the deploy console for 10 minutes after rollout completes. After that window, rollback requires a new deploy of the previous version.” [eng-deploy-runbook-2023, section “Rollback window”] It is outdated; the current in-force runbook gives a 45-minute window after full rollout completes. [eng-deploy-runbook, section “Rollback window”]

verdict: null
citations: {"eng-deploy-runbook-2023": "A deploy can be rolled back with a single click in the deploy console for 10 minutes after rollout completes. After that window, rollback requires a new deploy of the previous version.", "eng-deploy-runbook": "A deploy can be rolled back with a single click in the deploy console for 45 minutes after full rollout completes. After that window, rollback requires a new deploy of the previous version following the Rollback Procedure."}
